  "id": "Compound::DB00492 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Fosinopril and Slc15a1 through a series of molecular interactions involving Captopril and Perindopril. Fosinopril, an Ace Inhibitor, is linked to both Skull Hypoplasia and Oligohydramnios, which are conditions associated with Captopril, another Ace Inhibitor. Captopril binds to Slc15a1, indicating a direct interaction that may contribute to the observed effects. Similarly, Perindopril, an Ace Inhibitor, is associated with Serositis, which also binds to Slc15a1. The shared pathway through Ace Inhibitors and the common ancestor of Fosinopril and Captopril suggests a broader mechanism by which these drugs may influence Slc15a1. The evidence supports a possible role of these drugs in modulating Slc15a1 through their shared biochemical properties, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
